language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Four islands on a 2x2 map (A=0 north-west, B=1 north-east, C=2 south-west, D=3 south-east) each have a name, an export and a tourist attraction; find the assignment that satisfies the six clues.
find island : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..3)
find export : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..3)
find attraction : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..3)

branching on [island, export, attraction]

such that
$ each island has a different map position
allDiff(island),
$ each export is on a different island
allDiff(export),
$ each tourist attraction is on a different island
allDiff(attraction),
$ clue 1: the island with the koala preserve is due south of Pwana (same column, next row: position plus 2)
attraction[4] = island[1] + 2,
$ clue 2: the island with the largest alabaster quarry is due west of Quero (Quero is in the east column, so position minus 1)
(island[2] = 1 \/ island[2] = 3),
export[1] = island[2] - 1,
$ clue 3: the island with the resort hotel is due east of the island that exports durian fruit (durian is in the west column, so position plus 1)
(export[4] = 0 \/ export[4] = 2),
attraction[1] = export[4] + 1,
$ clue 4: Skern and the island with the jai alai stadium are connected by a north-south bridge (positions two apart)
(island[4] - attraction[3] = 2 \/ attraction[3] - island[4] = 2),
$ clue 5: Rayou and the island that exports bananas are connected by an east-west bridge (positions one apart in the same row)
(island[3] - export[2] = 1 \/ export[2] - island[3] = 1),
(island[3] / 2 = export[2] / 2),
$ clue 6: the ice skating rink and the jai alai stadium are not connected by a bridge (diagonal, distance 3)
|attraction[2] - attraction[3]| = 3
